Pac-Man /pacman feature — implementation reasoning

WHY the design choices (for future maintainers):

Engine model (discrete tile + progress fraction, not free pixels):
- Decisions (turns, pellet eating, ghost direction choice) happen exactly at
  tile centers. This removes floating-point alignment ambiguity, making every
  transition reproducible and unit-testable without a DOM.
- Determinism for "random" ghosts comes from a seeded LCG stored in GameState
  (rngState). Tests pass a fixed seed so ghost movement never flakes, while
  gameplay seeds from Date.now(). This satisfies the spec's v1 random strategy
  (random valid direction at intersections, no chase AI) AND testability.

Frame-delta clamping (MAX_STEP_MS):
- Backgrounding a tab produces a huge rAF delta on return. Clamping prevents
  the sim fast-forwarding/skipping. Combined with explicit + visibility pause.

React/canvas split:
- The engine state lives in a ref; React state mirrors only discrete HUD/
  overlay values (score, lives, phase). The rAF loop advances+draws every
  frame without triggering React re-renders. The rAF handle is stored in a ref
  and cancelled on cleanup so StrictMode's dev double-invoke can't spawn
  duplicate loops.

Maze generated procedurally (pillar maze) rather than hand-drawn ASCII:
- Single-tile wall pillars at (even,even) interior cells never disconnect the
  corridors, so the level is provably fully connected/solvable without manual
  verification. Tunnel = open border tiles on the middle row with column wrap.

Testing importance:
- Gameplay timing is non-deterministic in Playwright, so E2E asserts only on
  DOM/HUD/overlay state (start on input, restart resets, no Hello regression).
  All scoring/collision/frightened/win/game-over/tunnel rules are locked down
  by the 16 deterministic engine unit tests — these are the real safety net.
- test_pacman.py is strict-typed (FlaskClient[Any] + from __future__ import
  annotations) because the pre-commit mypy hook applies pyproject strict=true
  to staged test files (script/typecheck only covers src/).

Gotchas captured in AGENTS.md/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:
- Playwright uses getByLabel (not RTL's getByLabelText).
- script/server's Vite child can be SIGHUP'd; if it dies, islands fail with
  ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED to :5173 and every e2e reports the mount as "hidden".
- npx playwright install chromium needed (only ffmpeg cached).
